.Sh HISTORY
Support for OCB mode was added in OpenSSL 1.1.0.
.Pp
.Vt EVP_CIPHER_CTX
was made opaque in OpenSSL 1.1.0. As a result,
.Fn EVP_CIPHER_CTX_reset
appeared and
.Xr EVP_CIPHER_CTX_cleanup 3
disappeared.
.Xr EVP_CIPHER_CTX_init 3
remains as an alias for
.Fn EVP_CIPHER_CTX_reset .
.Pp
The
.Fn EVP_CIPHER_CTX_cipher
function was deprecated in OpenSSL 3.0; use
.Fn EVP_CIPHER_CTX_get0_cipher
instead.
.Pp
The
.Fn EVP_EncryptInit_ex2 ,
.Fn EVP_DecryptInit_ex2 ,
.Fn EVP_CipherInit_ex2 ,
.Fn EVP_CIPHER_fetch ,
.Fn EVP_CIPHER_free ,
.Fn EVP_CIPHER_up_ref ,
.Fn EVP_CIPHER_CTX_get0_cipher ,
.Fn EVP_CIPHER_CTX_get1_cipher ,
.Fn EVP_CIPHER_get_params ,
.Fn EVP_CIPHER_CTX_set_params ,
.Fn EVP_CIPHER_CTX_get_params ,
.Fn EVP_CIPHER_gettable_params ,
.Fn EVP_CIPHER_settable_ctx_params ,
.Fn EVP_CIPHER_gettable_ctx_params ,
.Fn EVP_CIPHER_CTX_settable_params
and
.Fn EVP_CIPHER_CTX_gettable_params
functions were added in 3.0.
.Pp
The
.Fn EVP_CIPHER_nid ,
.Fn EVP_CIPHER_name ,
.Fn EVP_CIPHER_block_size ,
.Fn EVP_CIPHER_key_length ,
.Fn EVP_CIPHER_iv_length ,
.Fn EVP_CIPHER_flags ,
.Fn EVP_CIPHER_mode ,
.Fn EVP_CIPHER_type ,
.Fn EVP_CIPHER_CTX_nid ,
.Fn EVP_CIPHER_CTX_block_size ,
.Fn EVP_CIPHER_CTX_key_length ,
.Fn EVP_CIPHER_CTX_iv_length ,
.Fn EVP_CIPHER_CTX_tag_length ,
.Fn EVP_CIPHER_CTX_num ,
.Fn EVP_CIPHER_CTX_type ,
and
.Fn EVP_CIPHER_CTX_mode
functions were renamed to include
.Qo Li get Qc
or
.Qo Li get0 Qc
in their names in OpenSSL 3.0, respectively.
The old names are kept as non-deprecated alias macros.
.Pp
The
.Fn EVP_CIPHER_CTX_encrypting
function was renamed to
.Fn EVP_CIPHER_CTX_is_encrypting
in OpenSSL 3.0. The old name is kept as non-deprecated alias macro.
.Pp
The
.Fn EVP_CIPHER_CTX_flags
macro was deprecated in OpenSSL 1.1.0.
.Pp
.Fn EVP_CIPHER_CTX_dup
was added in OpenSSL 3.2.
.Pp
.Fn EVP_CipherInit_SKEY
was added in OpenSSL 3.5.
.Pp
Prior to OpenSSL 3.5, passing a NULL
.Fa ctx
to
.Sy EVP_CIPHER_CTX_get_block_size()
would result in a NULL pointer dereference, rather than a 0 return value
indicating an error.
